<edge source="ai_safety_race::safety_incident_freq" target="brics_alignment_growth::geopolitical_alignment" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">High‑visibility safety failures in frontier AI systems developed or deployed by Western firms generate political distrust and regulatory backlash abroad, prompting some states to pivot diplomatically and economically toward alternative technology partners in the BRICS bloc that promise different risk governance or onshore options.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_safety_race</data>
  <data key="d39">brics_alignment_growth</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ai_safety_race::safety_incident_freq" target="global_rate_shock::market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in frontier-AI safety incidents (e.g., model-driven trading errors, data-poisoning, or automated-misconduct) causes counterparties and automated market-makers to withdraw from markets and triggers trading halts, directly reducing depth and widening spreads.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">ai_safety_race</data>
  <data key="d39">global_rate_shock</data>
</edge>
