<edge source="global_rate_shock::long_term_nominal_yields" target="ai_safety_race::average_model_capability" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.7</data>
  <data key="d36">Rising long-term yields increase the hurdle rate for long‑duration capital expenditures, reducing willingness to finance large compute clusters and sustained training campaigns, which lowers the average capability of frontier models produced.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_rate_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_safety_race</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_rate_shock::long_term_nominal_yields" target="brics_alignment_growth::investment_divergence" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">A sustained rise in long-term nominal yields raises the global cost of capital unevenly, making projects in higher‑cost markets less attractive and prompting asymmetric capital allocation that widens investment flow divergence across rival regions.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_rate_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">brics_alignment_growth</data>
</edge>
<edge source="global_rate_shock::long_term_nominal_yields" target="russia_ukraine_conflict::energy_supply_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">+</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.65</data>
  <data key="d36">A spike in long‑term yields increases refinancing costs and insurance premiums for energy traders and infrastructure owners, delaying repairs to damaged pipelines/terminals and constraining credit‑financed fuel imports, thereby increasing energy supply disruptions in the conflict zone.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">global_rate_shock</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_conflict</data>
</edge>
