<edge source="brics_alignment_growth::cross_border_capital" target="ai_safety_race::frontier_dev_speed" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Large net capital flows away from incumbent AI hubs reduce venture funding, cloud credits and M&amp;A activity for frontier teams, cutting R&amp;D budgets and slowing the pace of new high‑capability model development.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">brics_alignment_growth</data>
  <data key="d39">ai_safety_race</data>
</edge>
<edge source="brics_alignment_growth::cross_border_capital" target="global_rate_shock::market_liquidity" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">3</data>
  <data key="d35">0.75</data>
  <data key="d36">A rapid intensification of cross-border capital movements (net outflows from particular sovereign bond markets toward rival blocs) drains dealer inventories and order-book depth in those markets, widening bid-ask spreads and reducing market liquidity.</data>
  <data key="d37">0-6 months</data>
  <data key="d38">brics_alignment_growth</data>
  <data key="d39">global_rate_shock</data>
</edge>
<edge source="brics_alignment_growth::cross_border_capital" target="russia_ukraine_conflict::energy_supply_disruption" id="0">
  <data key="d27">cross_causal</data>
  <data key="d33">-</data>
  <data key="d28">2</data>
  <data key="d35">0.6</data>
  <data key="d36">Increased inward capital flows to Russian energy and logistics firms finance repairs, spare‑parts imports and alternative export arrangements, thereby reducing the occurrence and duration of energy supply disruptions.</data>
  <data key="d37">6-18 months</data>
  <data key="d38">brics_alignment_growth</data>
  <data key="d39">russia_ukraine_conflict</data>
</edge>
